   "w": 776,
   "text": "675 pts · 273 comments · 1 d · RohanAdwankar",
   "size": "xs"
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "x": 12,
   "y": 128,
   "w": 776,
   "text": "Any hits? Do models even know their own weights to be able to do this? Probably\nyes, because they have been presumably trained on their own output and\nconversations about themselves.",
   "lines": 3
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "x": 12,
   "y": 215,
   "w": 776,
   "text": "No, they would probably have to hack the internal system of the company running\nthem. It would not be a particularly wide ranging hack. There is a strong likelihood\nof the weights being on the actual machine that is running the model.",
   "lines": 3
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "x": 12,
   "y": 302,
   "w": 776,
   "text": "It is something that I have wondered about with models like these. How many\nphysical locations are needed to serve a model on that scale? Do they have a huge\nnumber of sites running inference?",
   "lines": 3
  },
